Required regressions before applying this staged patch:

1. an exactly zero score vector returns `{}`, count zero, and
   `AllScoresZero -> True`;
2. an all-nonzero score vector of width `n` returns `Range[n]` and count `n`;
3. a mixed score vector returns exactly the one-based nonzero positions;
4. every returned index lies in `1 ;; columns` and the count never exceeds
   the candidate width;
5. the frozen V6d and RAD9 artifacts remain admissible as historical evidence,
   while replayed score metadata loses only the spurious index zero.

Do not apply while the source-pinned CF300 V5 mission is active.  The bug is
conservative for the existing conclusions: it forced the full two-rank path.
